From 2e9b6803b33054b0cce27e72ec9b36688416f6f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:47:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/36] generate: STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP's gate and pre-read
 setup, checked per batched prompt segment (dry run)

With STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP=1 and a pipelined batch, each batched prompt segment of an admission beside decoding slots
is now checked live (overlap_gate) and prepared (overlap_prepare), then still read as before with the slots drained:
"strata batch: overlapped read eligible: tokens A..B", or once per reason "strata batch: overlapped read off: <why>".
The overlapped read itself comes next. Env off: none of the new code runs (the refactors below are identical).

- Prefill: ple_on_/ple_batched_ (run_impl's predicate factored out unchanged, read live), device(), overlap_safe()
  over the chain, chain_cuda_error() (each later stage's chunk thread keeps the first sticky CUDA error it ends
  with; reset per run).
- Verifier: set_stream_priority_high (before init; greatest priority, a normal stream when that fails; not on HIP),
  ar_live(), has_batch_layout(), ensure_batch_layouts() (stage_batch's capture of the full-width group layouts, ahead,
  respecting --batch-mtp's graph limit; the commit graph uploaded too), set_no_capture() (stage_batch then fails
  instead of capturing).
- MtpDrafter: reserve_prefill_records(n) (prefill()'s record growth for n rows and every 1..max_t prompt graph,
  of the STRATA_MTP_PREFILL_SYNC variant in use), set_stream_priority() before load.
- Knobs (env on only): STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_PRIO (default 1: every stage verifier's window stream at the greatest
  priority), STRATA_PIPE_OVERLAP_MTP_PRIO (unset: as before; 1/0: the drafter's stream at the greatest/default).

The gate, decided per condition by what the read and the windows would share (none of them refuses the production
T16 config: split 12,24,36, --ple-io ram, own prompt buffers):
- a batch admission (admit_slot), nothing in flight;
- no prompt loan (pf_parts first/lent): a lent slot holds prompt buffers and its expert runs on the CPU;
- residency live, not the startup const: every host_res entry >= 0, no pending swap, and every stage's ar_live()
  (its zero-doorbell graph; T_main then never serves a doorbell or the CPU pool during a read);
- refused: --kv-resident (the prompt's K/V staging lives in expert slots), pictures (untested: vision rows and their
  positions), --peer-device, remote expert caches, foresight swaps, a control vector, the elastic K/V (added; it
  evicts experts), STRATA_IDX_FP16_CHECK / STRATA_CVEC_FUSE_CHECK (lazy statics), --ple-sync-submit (the reader is
  then not thread-safe), the first prompt stage on another card than stage 1;
- Prefill::overlap_safe on every stage: no peer, no stage helper, no CPU pool, own buffers (added), no K/V
  streaming (added), and the PLE block batched (the per-token block writes the session's PLE scratch, which the
  stage-0 windows write).
Deviations from the design: the drafter's prompt graphs were assumed captured by prepare_prefill, which only
--pipeline-windows calls; they are captured lazily on the last stage's thread, so reserve_prefill_records captures
them (both STRATA_MTP_PREFILL_SYNC variants, so that env needs no refusal). The drafter's stream is at the default
priority without --pipeline-windows, so MTP_PRIO is 1/0 (raise/default), not "normal". Verifier::device() existed.

Checked (T16-mmqtab.json, 12,24,36, 4 groups of 4, STRATA_MMQ_DIRECT=1, --pcie-frac 0 --adapt-every 1000000
--no-prefill-borrow, tools/batch_test16.py 16 slots x 64 tokens with a 1200-token last prompt): the reference engine,
this build env off, env on, env on with MTP_PRIO=1: solo and batch tokens identical in all four (and to M1's), every
slot equal to solo. Env on logs one "eligible" (the 1164-token read; the short prompts go through windows) after
"captured 12 full-width group layouts in 24.3 ms"; no "not captured before an overlapped read". Refusals reproduced,
each once and with batch == solo: STRATA_PLE_BATCH=0, --kv-resident 8192, STRATA_PREFILL_HELP=1,
STRATA_SPLIT_OWN_BUFFERS=0 (a loan), --ple-io direct --ple-sync-submit, STRATA_VERIFY_ALL_RESIDENT=0 (the residency
check). STRATA_IDX_FP16_CHECK=1 crashes the solo path on this split in the reference engine too, so that refusal is
not reachable here. tools/batch_interleave_test.py (3 groups of 1): reference and env on print the same lines
(the 4888-token read eligible). The M0 driver with the production flags and env on: all 30 batched reads eligible,
one 16-layout capture (54 ms), the reads' medians as in M0 (153 tokens 199.8 vs 201.0 ms, 1219 tokens 609.2 vs
608.9 ms). No HIP toolchain here: the HIP paths are guarded like mtp.cpp's priority code, not compiled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
